<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hulbuk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hulbuk is the site of a medieval city in southern Tajikistan, at Kurbonshahid near Vose, identified as the capital of the principality of Khuttal. Its citadel and palace, excavated from the mid-20th century, flourished in the 9th to 12th centuries under the local rulers of Khuttal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanids</a> and Ghaznavids, and yielded fine carved and painted stucco decoration. A reconstructed gate now stands at the site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hulbuk.jpg" alt="Hulbuk" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ninara from Helsinki, Finland · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Town_Khulbuk,_Tajikistan_(28912837737).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
